<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kahaya II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1895">1895</a>–<a href="/years/1944">1944</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kahaya II was Omugabe, or king, of Ankole from 1895 to 1944. He was installed young after the succession conflict that followed the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ntare-v">Ntare V</a>, with the backing of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuwa-mbaguta">Nuwa Mbaguta</a>, who as chief minister held much of the real power. Under him the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ankole-agreement">Ankole Agreement</a> of 1901 placed the kingdom within the British Uganda <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a>, and it became a colonial district with appointed chiefs and a headquarters at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mbarara">Mbarara</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kahaya-ii.jpg" alt="Kahaya II" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kahaya_II_and_his_counsellors.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
